From b41b4b6af0131c49668c814ad49c7c0c03e7cc9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:00:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] flashnext: the kv-cache fp8 and row-cache levers' files
 compile

Nine defects the fp8 and pread levers landed in files their lanes never compiled: the fp8 glue's
three On helpers take the Glue they never read, the fp8 attnChunksOn passes its shared-byte count
as the wider type its launch takes, the prompt row cache's import block was written twice, its open
hands the Ngram by value where the reader takes a pointer and names ple's shard bound privately,
the row cache test's two opens discard the reader they then unwrap and call the pool's ahead free
function as a method, the n-gram pool the reader creates is never destroyed by the Ngram's deinit,
the snap sizing reads a Kv the file never imported and calls its own attnBytes with the old
two-argument shape, the paging batch test's Fake lacks the fp8 calls the batched pass now routes
to, and the draft head's KV rows lost their cap: the kv-cache squash priced and allocated one
position's rows where the head's cache holds the window's, a window short of the thirteen caches
the kv8 test and the snapshot moves price. No record or launch changes; every reply is the tree's
own and the knobs stay off by default.
